# Frontend command harness

There is exactly one command to run any build/test/lint/check action across
`frontend-web`, `frontend-admin` and `packages/*`:

```
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs <action> [--package <path>] [-- <extra args>]
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs --help   # lists every <action> and whether it needs --package
```

Never call `pnpm`/`npm`/`yarn`/`npx` directly for one of these actions —
`.cursor/hooks/enforce-frontend-commands.mjs` denies it, correctly formed or
not, and names the exact wrapper command to use instead. This is not a style
preference the agent is trusted to remember; it is enforced before the
command runs.

## Why a wrapper, not just a documented pnpm command

Two problems a written convention alone doesn't solve:

1. **The agent shouldn't be the one deciding how a check is invoked.** A menu
   of "correct" pnpm forms per action is still a menu — a `--filter` by
   package name instead of path is exactly the class of mistake
   `.github/scripts/README.md` already documents as a real, shipped bug. A
   single script removes the choice instead of hoping it's made correctly
   every time.
2. **Raw tool output is expensive.** `tsc`, `eslint`, `vitest`, `playwright`
   and `next build` each produce their own verbose format, none of it meant
   for a context window. The wrapper always writes the full output to a log
   file and prints only a compact digest to stdout: `OK <action>` on
   success, or a handful of `file:line — message` lines plus the log path on
   failure.

## What the wrapper does internally

`.cursor/lib/actions.mjs` is the single source of truth both the wrapper and
the hook read from — this is not duplicated between them:

- **`repo-only`** actions (`lint`, `lint:fix`, `verify`) run `pnpm run
  <action>` — only the root defines them; `--package` is rejected.
- **`repo-or-package`** actions (`typecheck`, `arch`, `test`, `build`,
  `tokens:generate`, `tokens:check`) run `pnpm run <action>` with no
  `--package`, fanning out to every workspace member that defines it, or
  `pnpm --filter "./<path>" run <action>` with one.
- **`package-only`** actions (the browser suites — `test:e2e`, `test:visual`,
  `test:visual:update`, `test:a11y`, `test:contrast`, `test:contrast:wcag`,
  `test:contrast:apca`, `test:scoped`, `test:mutation`, `graph`, `storybook`,
  `build-storybook`) require `--package <path>` — there is no root form.

Package scoping is always by path (`--filter "./frontend-web"`, never
`--filter tallyvane-frontend-web` or `cd frontend-web &&`), for a reason
that's been measured, not assumed: `pnpm --filter "./frontend-web"`,
`pnpm --filter tallyvane-frontend-web`, and `cd frontend-web && pnpm run`
all took the same ~624ms for an equivalent no-op — pnpm resolves the whole
workspace graph regardless of selector kind, so there's no performance case
for name-based or `cd`-based scoping. There is a stability case against it: a
`package.json` `name` routinely diverges from its folder (`frontend-web` →
`tallyvane-frontend-web`, `packages/design-tokens` → `design-token-engine`,
`packages/storybook` → `tallyvane-storybook`), which is exactly the bug
`.github/scripts/README.md` documents. The `./` prefix is load-bearing, not
cosmetic — `pnpm --filter frontend-web` (no leading `./`) and `pnpm --filter
packages/storybook` both fail to match anything at all; verified directly,
not assumed.

## Examples

```bash
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs verify
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs typecheck --package packages/frontend-shared
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs test:e2e --package frontend-web
node .cursor/cli/agent-check.mjs test:scoped --package packages/storybook -- visual.spec.ts -g "Button"
```

## What the hook still allows unchanged

Anything that isn't running one of the actions above through a package
manager: `git`, `pnpm install`, `pnpm add`/`why`/`list`, dev servers
(`pnpm run dev`, out of this harness's scope on purpose), and a narrowly
scoped debug command like `npx eslint src/foo.ts` (one file, not a substitute
for the real check). Only a bare, argument-less `npx eslint` / `npx tsc
--noEmit` / `npx playwright test` / `node_modules/.bin/vitest` — standing in
for the whole check — is denied.
